SUMMARY:2026 Conference on Global Indigenous Studies (CGIS)
DESCRIPTION:CGIS 2026 is a transdisciplinary event that will bring togeth
 er national and international scholars\, educators\, practitioners\, stud
 ents\, policy makers\, activists\, academic institutions\, Indigenous org
 anizations\, grassroots organizations\, governmental and non-governmental
  organizations. The participants in this conference will be involved in a
  local and global dialogue and exchange of ideas\, research\, and experie
 nces on the themes of the event.  Across the globe\, ethnic minorities an
 d Indigenous communities have consistently strived to protect their rich 
 cultural heritages and linguistic nuances from the influences of colonial
  powers\, expanding nation-states\, and the homogenizing impact of global
 ization. This collective effort is increasingly recognized\, highlighted 
 by the initiation of UNESCO's "Indigenous Languages Decade" (2022-2032) (
 https://www.unesco.org/en/decades/indigenous-languages/community/adhocgro
 ups). The imperative acknowledgment is that Indigenous languages\, along 
 with the intricate knowledge systems interwoven within them\, stand as cr
 ucial pillars for preserving both biological and cultural pluralism.Regis
 tration Costs (https://indianauniv.ungerboeck.com/prod/emc00/register.asp
 x?aat=2f74415350355073564f6a6a762f4163555748484461566c746378794d6f4d4d674
 44739715679693634733d)  Early Bird Registration: $60.00 (Before October 1
 \, 2026)  Standard Registration: $80.00 (October 1 - November 15\, 2026) 
  &#160\;2026 Keynote Speakers:  Aluki Kotierk  Armando Muyolema  Diego A.
  Titueña Matango  Teresa L. McCarty  &#160\;  Conference on Global and I
 ndigenous Studies (CGIS) is made possible by the support from:&#160\;Afri
 can Studies Program (https://africanstudies.indiana.edu/index.html?_gl=1*
 4pv3u5*_gcl_au*MTI2NDk4MTcxLjE3NzUwNTYwNjQ.*_ga*MTUxNzYzNjMwOS4xNzc1MDU2M
 DUw*_ga_61CH0D2DQW*czE3NzY5Njg4MDEkbzMzJGcwJHQxNzc2OTY4ODAxJGo2MCRsMCRoMA
 ..)Arts and Humanities Futures – Indigenous Futures at IUB (https://ahf
 utures.iu.edu/)Center for Latin American and Caribbean Studies (https://c
 lacs.indiana.edu/index.html)Center for the Study of the Middle East (http
 s://csme.indiana.edu/index.html)East Asian Studies Center (https://easc.i
 ndiana.edu/index.html)Inner Asian and Uralic National Resource Center (ht
 tps://iaunrc.indiana.edu/index.html)The Byrnes Institute (REEI) (https://
 reei.indiana.edu/index.html)IU Global (https://global.iu.edu/index.html)I
 nstitute for Indigenous Knowledge (https://indigenousknowledge.indiana.ed
 u/index.html)Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies (h
 ttps://hamiltonlugar.indiana.edu/)      &#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>CGIS 2026</strong> is a transdisc
 iplinary event that will bring together national and international schola
 rs\, educators\, practitioners\, students\, policy makers\, activists\, a
 cademic institutions\, Indigenous organizations\, grassroots organization
 s\, governmental and non-governmental organizations. The participants in 
 this conference will be involved in a local and global dialogue and excha
 nge of ideas\, research\, and experiences on the themes of the event.</p>
 <p>  Across the globe\, ethnic minorities and Indigenous communities have
  consistently strived to protect their rich cultural heritages and lingui
 stic nuances from the influences of colonial powers\, expanding nation-st
 ates\, and the homogenizing impact of globalization. This collective effo
 rt is increasingly recognized\, highlighted by the initiation of <a class
 ="external" href="https://www.unesco.org/en/decades/indigenous-languages/
 community/adhocgroups">UNESCO's "Indigenous Languages Decade" (2022-2032)
 </a>. The imperative acknowledgment is that Indigenous languages\, along 
 with the intricate knowledge systems interwoven within them\, stand as cr
 ucial pillars for preserving both biological and cultural pluralism.</p><
 p><em><strong><a href="https://indianauniv.ungerboeck.com/prod/emc00/regi
