LOCATION:GISB Atrium
SUMMARY:Finding Home: Arts & Refugees Shining the Light
DESCRIPTION:The exhibit features images of and created by refugees in Eur
 ope.&#160\; Charlotte Schmitz's polaroid images of refugees who embarked 
 on the dangerous journey into Europe searching for a new home are annotat
 ed by the subjects of the images\, making a collaborative form of visual 
 documentary.&#160\; In addition\, images created by refugee children in V
 ienna express their hope for a better life.  The exhibition will culminat
 e in a dramatic reading of Deborah Haber's "Moses Man: Finding Home."&#16
 0\; Click here for more information: https://events.iu.edu/csme/event/247
 6138-moses-man-finding-home (https://events.iu.edu/csme/event/2476138-mos
 es-man-finding-home)&#160\;&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The exhibit features images of and crea
 ted by refugees in Europe.&#160\; Charlotte Schmitz's polaroid images of 
 refugees who embarked on the dangerous journey into Europe searching for 
 a new home are annotated by the subjects of the images\, making a collabo
 rative form of visual documentary.&#160\; In addition\, images created by
  refugee children in Vienna express their hope for a better life.</p><p> 
  The exhibition will culminate in a dramatic reading of Deborah Haber's "
 Moses Man: Finding Home."&#160\; Click here for more information: <a href
 ="https://events.iu.edu/csme/event/2476138-moses-man-finding-home">https:
 //events.iu.edu/csme/event/2476138-moses-man-finding-home</a>&#160\;&#160
 \;</p>
