LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Moses Man: Finding Home
DESCRIPTION:Written by Deborah Haber\, directed by Joe Calarco\, with mus
 ical direction by Casey Filiaci\, "Moses Man: Finding Home" presents the 
 true story of Haber's parents who fled their home in Vienna\, spending ye
 ars as refugees in Cyprus\, Palestine\, Nyasaland\, and South Africa\, be
 fore finally finding a new home in the United States.&#160\; The play exp
 lores the themes of forced displacement and migration by connecting Haber
 's parents' story to recent refugee stories.&#160\; Still in development\
 , the evening will feature a dramatic reading of the musical.&#160\; Cosp
 onsored by the Center for the Study of the Middle East and the Center for
  Caribbean and Latin American Studies\, with additional support from the 
 IU Institute for Advanced Study and the College Arts &amp\; Humanities In
 stitute\, the African Studies Program\, the Borns Jewish Studies Program\
 , and the Institute for European Studies.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Written by Deborah Haber\, directed by 
 Joe Calarco\, with musical direction by Casey Filiaci\, "Moses Man: Findi
 ng Home" presents the true story of Haber's parents who fled their home i
 n Vienna\, spending years as refugees in Cyprus\, Palestine\, Nyasaland\,
  and South Africa\, before finally finding a new home in the United State
 s.&#160\; The play explores the themes of forced displacement and migrati
 on by connecting Haber's parents' story to recent refugee stories.&#160\;
  Still in development\, the evening will feature a dramatic reading of th
 e musical.&#160\; Cosponsored by the Center for the Study of the Middle E
 ast and the Center for Caribbean and Latin American Studies\, with additi
 onal support from the IU Institute for Advanced Study and the College Art
 s &amp\; Humanities Institute\, the African Studies Program\, the Borns J
 ewish Studies Program\, and the Institute for European Studies.</p>
UID:20261115T000000Z-2482450@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20261112T133008Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2476138-moses-man-finding-home
CATEGORIES:Performances, shows, and films
LAST-MODIFIED:20261112T183008Z
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2482450
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>pearsonc@iu.edu</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>Moses Man: Finding Home tells the true stories of 
 forcibly displaced people: from the Holocaust\, from civil war\, from vio
 lence.&#160\; This presentation of Deborah Haber's musical\, a show that 
 examines the universality of displacement and the fragility of belonging 
 by weaving the true story of the Haber family fleeing Vienna during WWII 
 with the story of present-day Syrian and African refugees.</p>
END:VEVENT
