SUMMARY:Documentary Film "CREATIVE RESOLVE: The Future of Global Health"
DESCRIPTION:This film explores the transformative power of creative resol
 ve in global health. From the frontlines of Rwanda's HIV fight to the his
 toric eradication of smallpox\, it goes behind the scenes with the activi
 sts and experts who refused to accept the status quo. It's more than a hi
 story of medicine\; it's a blueprint for a future where health is a right
 \, not a privilege\, and international solidarity is our strongest vaccin
 e.  &#160\;Screening followed by a panel discussion and Q&amp\;A:  &#160\
 ;Nicole Hassoun  Professor\, Department of International Studies  Hamilto
 n Lugar School of Global and International Studies  Director\, Global Hea
 lth Impact Project  &#160\;Molly Rosenberg  Professor\, Department of Epi
 demiology and Biostatistics  IU School of Public Health\, Bloomington  &#
 160\;Julia Sherry (Moderator)  Lecturer\, Department of Applied Health Sc
 ience  Director\, Global Health  IU School of Public Health\, Bloomington
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This film explores the transformative p
 ower of creative resolve in global health. From the frontlines of Rwanda'
 s HIV fight to the historic eradication of smallpox\, it goes behind the 
 scenes with the activists and experts who refused to accept the status qu
 o. It's more than a history of medicine\; it's a blueprint for a future w
 here health is a right\, not a privilege\, and international solidarity i
 s our strongest vaccine.</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><strong>Screening followed
  by a panel discussion and Q&amp\;A:</strong></p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><stro
 ng>Nicole Hassoun</strong></p><p>  Professor\, Department of Internationa
 l Studies</p><p>  Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studi
 es</p><p>  Director\, Global Health Impact Project</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>
 <strong>Molly Rosenberg</strong></p><p>  Professor\, Department of Epidem
 iology and Biostatistics</p><p>  IU School of Public Health\, Bloomington
 </p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><strong>Julia Sherry</strong> (Moderator)</p><p>  
 Lecturer\, Department of Applied Health Science</p><p>  Director\, Global
  Health</p><p>  IU School of Public Health\, Bloomington</p>
