GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Lecture: A Failure of Will: Why Cyber Operations Against Ukraine'
 s and Poland's Energy Systems Go Unanswered with Szymon Skalski
DESCRIPTION:Cyber operations against power grids and heating systems recu
 r in war and outside it. The same conduct falls under the law of armed co
 nflict in one setting\, peacetime international law in the other. Drawing
  on Russian operations in Ukraine and Poland\, this lecture asks why corr
 ect legal classification so rarely brings consequences.  Szymon Skalski i
 s a doctoral candidate at Jagiellonian University and Visiting Scholar at
  IU's Ostrom Workshop\, where he leads its working group on environmental
  security and technological risk in conflict. His research interests incl
 ude cybersecurity of critical infrastructure\, global security\, and liab
 ility for cyberattacks.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">
 Cyber operations against power grids and heating systems recur in war and
  outside it. The same conduct falls under the law of armed conflict in on
 e setting\, peacetime international law in the other. Drawing on Russian 
 operations in Ukraine and Poland\, this lecture asks why correct legal cl
 assification so rarely brings consequences.</span></p><p class="x_element
 ToProof" data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">  Szymon Skalski is a doctora
 l candidate at Jagiellonian University and Visiting Scholar at IU's Ostro
 m Workshop\, where he leads its working group on environmental security a
 nd technological risk in conflict. His research interests include cyberse
 curity of critical infrastructure\, global security\, and liability for c
 yberattacks.</p>
