SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: International Cris
 is Response Simulation — Leading Under Pressure
DESCRIPTION:Master the Tradecraft of Crisis Leadership  When internationa
 l crises break\, leaders don't have the luxury of complete information or
  total control. They have to make rapid strategic calls\, counter targete
 d disinformation in real time\, and align rival organizations under inten
 se scrutiny.  Skip the slides and build actual operational skills in Inte
 rnational Crisis Response\, an interactive\, multi-agency simulation desi
 gned to test and sharpen your leadership under realistic pressure.  Guide
 d by Michael Jack\, certified leadership coach\, international disaster s
 trategist\, and former USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance Division 
 Director\, this hands-on session pushes you beyond theory into real-world
  strategic execution.  Core Skills You'll Walk Away WithRapid Strategic D
 ecision-Making: Practice making consequential\, high-level decisions unde
 r extreme time pressure and incomplete data.    Crisis Communications &am
 p\; Disinformation Defense: Learn how to deliver disciplined messaging un
 der scrutiny\, navigate press briefings\, and actively counter viral fake
  news.    Cross-Organizational Negotiation: Master coalition-building and
  gap-filling across international teams\, host governments\, UN bodies\, 
 and non-profits whose interests may compete with your own.    Leadership 
 Resilience &amp\; Trauma Management: Gain practical tools for managing st
 aff decision fatigue\, operational stress\, and team performance during p
 rolonged high-pressure events.      Dynamic Roleplay Structure  You'll be
  embedded directly into key crisis response teams—representing U.S. Emb
 assy officials\, UN agencies\, international NGOs\, host government autho
 rities\, and global media correspondents—responding live as dynamic sce
 nario "injects" unfold.  ߌࠗho Can Attend?Open to all: Undergrads\, Gra
 d Students\, Faculty\, Staff\, and Community Members. (Light snacks and d
 rinks provided)  Facilitator Bio  Michael Jack is a certified leadership 
 coach\, international crisis management strategist\, and former Division 
 Director at USAID's Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance. He has managed di
 saster responses across 80+ countries\, including the Iraq Sinjar crisis\
 , West Africa Ebola outbreak\, Mexico City earthquake\, South Sudan emerg
 ency\, Amazon wildfires\, and Northern Ethiopia response.
